# Product-molecularity fixture: 100 rings A.B.C (B and C also bonded to each
# other) and 100 linear A.B.C. The rule deletes A's bonds to B and to C and
# claims three products. On a ring B and C stay bonded, so the products never
# separate: BNG2.pl's network reacts only the linear species, and Ring stays 100.
# Testing only the ends of each deleted bond (A-B, A-C) missed it.
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,c)
  C(a,b)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c!3).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,a!3) 100
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,b) 100
end seed species
begin observables
  Species Ring A(b!1,c!3).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,a!3)
  Molecules Afree A(b,c)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1).C(a!2) -> A(b,c) + B(a) + C(a) k
end reaction rules
end model
writeXML()
